Author: b <a@b>
Date:   Tue Oct 13 11:34:30 2026 -0700

    REFACTOR-0002: JsonBookingStore adapts fs to the core's BookingStore
    
    The core declares the BookingStore port in its own terms: a room's
    bookings on a date, and add a booking. Node's fs can't implement that,
    so JsonBookingStore adapts it, the same way SpotifyAdapter adapted the
    Spotify SDK to MusicSource. Reading the file, the format version, and
    writing it back moved here from src/bookings.ts, and nothing else knows
    about them.
    
    run() books through the core's book() with the store it's given.
    main.ts is left with the jobs at the edge: read argv, word the answer,
    and pick the real store. It's the one place that names
    JsonBookingStore.
    
    src/bookings.ts and its FakeFileSystem tests are gone: the rules are
    tested in the core, without a file format. test/architecture.spec.ts
    still passes, so the core still imports nothing from outside src/core.

